, used to prove a node is on an unconfirmable branch and can be rejected"}},"removeOldZombies(uint256)":{"params":{"startIndex":"Index in the zombie list to start removing zombies from (to limit the cost of this transaction)"}},"removeZombie(uint256,uint256)":{"params":{"maxNodes":"Maximum number of nodes to remove the zombie from (to limit the cost of this transaction)","zombieNum":"Index of the zombie to remove"}},"requiredStake(uint256,uint64,uint64)":{"details":"If the stake requirement get's too high, this function may start reverting due to overflow, but that only blocks operations that should be blocked anyway","returns":{"_0":"The current minimum stake requirement"}},"returnOldDeposit(address)":{"details":"Since a staker is initially placed in the latest confirmed node, if they don't move it a griefer can remove their stake. It is recomended to batch together the txs to place a stake and move it to the desired node.","params":{"stakerAddress":"Address of the staker whose stake is refunded"}},"stakeOnExistingNode(uint64,bytes32)":{"params":{"nodeHash":"Node hash of nodeNum (protects against reorgs)","nodeNum":"Index of the node to move stake to. This must by a child of the node the staker is currently staked on"}},"stakeOnNewNode((((bytes32[2],uint64[2]),uint8),((bytes32[2],uint64[2]),uint8),uint64),bytes32,uint256)":{"params":{"assertion":"The assertion data","expectedNodeHash":"The hash of the node being created (protects against reorgs)"}},"stakerCount()":{"returns":{"_0":"Number of active stakers currently staked"}},"withdrawableFunds(address)":{"params":{"user":"Address to check the funds of"},"returns":{"_0":"Amount of funds withdrawable by user"}},"zombieAddress(uint256)":{"params":{"zombieNum":"Index of the zombie to lookup"},"returns":{"_0":"Original staker address of the zombie"}},"zombieCount()":{"returns":{"_0":"Current number of un-removed zombies"}},"zombieLatestStakedNode(uint256)":{"params":{"zombieNum":"Index of the zombie to lookup"},"return